From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Lehmann <dlehmann@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:50:35 +0200
Subject: [objects] Forbid adding private symbols to Wasm objects

Wasm objects have a fixed layout and must not transition their maps.
Harden LookupIterator::ExtendingNonExtensible by generally disallowing
map transitions for Wasm objects. This matches the existing check for
shared objects. This causes private symbol stores on Wasm objects to
throw a TypeError instead of transitioning their map.

